Release Notes — v0.8.1.34.1
Purpose

Preserve Scenario B soft-throttle behavior by preventing legacy marginal-day logic from re-introducing a hard DAY_GATE block.

This version is a correctness + invariance fix, not a signal change.

What Changed (Single Behavior Fix)
Scenario B only

DAY_GATE consequence is now fully standardized as a soft throttle

Legacy marginal-day override logic can no longer re-enable effective_day_gate_failed=True

Only exception preserved: marginal_stop_after_1_loss (v0.8.1.17.0) may halt trading after an SL on marginal days (by design)

A new invariant now holds:

Once Scenario B soft throttle is active, DAY_GATE will not hard-block entries again during the day.

What Did NOT Change

DAY_GATE prepass logic

Day classification (healthy / marginal / hostile)

VWAP logic

Marginal VWAP window logic

VWAP extension gate

Post-damage guards

Confirm-bar logic

Risk model (only throttle scaling already in place)

Non-B scenarios

Observability Added

New log (once per day when applicable):

[WHY] v0.8.1.34.1 B_SOFT_THROTTLE_OVERRIDES_LEGACY_MARGINAL


Confirms that soft throttle is actively overriding legacy marginal behavior.

Validation Performed
Sanity cluster (Scenario B)

2025-08-05 → 2025-08-07

Results:

Aug 05: 0 trades (blocked by entry guards, not DAY_GATE)

Aug 06: 2 trades (1 TP, 1 SL), soft throttle correctly allowed participation

Aug 07: 0 trades (hostile day; post-damage + VWAP guards correctly blocked)

Key confirmation:

DAY_GATE is no longer a participation bottleneck

Soft throttle invariant holds across marginal and hostile days

Conclusion

v0.8.1.34.1 successfully removes DAY_GATE as a latent choke point and restores correct Cameron-style regime handling for Scenario B.

This version is complete and safe to tag.

Handover Notes — Start of v0.8.1.35.0
Context

As of v0.8.1.34.1:

Scenario B regime control is now correct

Soft throttle works as intended

Legacy marginal logic no longer interferes

Remaining lack of participation is not caused by DAY_GATE

Current System State (Important)

Scenario B

DAY_GATE → soft throttle (working)

Marginal days → capped participation (working)

Hostile days → protected by post-damage + VWAP logic (working)

Dominant remaining blockers (observed in logs):

MARGINAL_VWAP_WINDOW_REJECT (very frequent)

VWAP_EXTENSION_BLOCK

Post-damage continuation rules (hostile days)

Open Problem (Carried Forward)

Participation on marginal days is now limited primarily by VWAP-related entry guards, not by regime gating.

This is a signal-quality tuning problem, not a safety or regime problem.

Next Version Hypothesis (v0.8.1.35.0)

Marginal-day participation is overly suppressed by the Marginal VWAP Window gate, even when structure and regime are acceptable.

Scope Rules for v0.8.1.35.0

One lever only

Must affect marginal days only

Must not weaken hostile-day protection

Candidate levers (choose one explicitly):

Marginal VWAP window behavior
or

VWAP extension cap on marginal days

Validation Pattern (Must Follow)
Sanity cluster

2025-08-05 → 2025-08-07 (Scenario B)

Protection cluster

2025-12-02 → 2025-12-05 (Scenario B)

No additional days unless behavior is ambiguous.

Start Condition for v0.8.1.35.0

Before writing any code, state explicitly:

“This version tests whether marginal-day VWAP entry rules are overly restrictive, using Aug 05–07 as sanity and Dec 02–05 as protection.”